{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.heisenberg_commutator","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.heisenberg_commutator","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.heisenberg_commutator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.heisenberg_commutator","kind":"theorem","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse/heisenberg_commutator.lean#L42-L59","doc":"**Proposition** (heisenberg commutator):\n\nLet `q : ℝ` be the substrate parameter and `J : ℝ` the\ncomplex-structure scalar.  With `ℏ_q(q) = 1 − q⁻¹` and\n`[X̂, P̂]_q = J · ℏ_q`, the manuscript identities hold and the classical\nlimit `q = 1 → [X̂, P̂]_q = 0` follows by computation.\n\n* `hbarQ q = 1 − q⁻¹` — by definition;\n* `commutator_q q J = J · ℏ_q` — by definition;\n* `q = 1 → commutator_q q J = 0` — **derived**: `ℏ_q(1) = 0`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:heisenberg-commutator","label":"prop:heisenberg-commutator","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/heisenberg-commutator-prop.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.commutator_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.commutator_q","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse/heisenberg_commutator.lean#L38-L40","doc":"The `q`-deformed commutator `[X̂, P̂]_q = J · ℏ_q(q)` — **defined**\nfrom `J` and `q` via the manuscript identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.hbarQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanUniverse.hbarQ","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ArchimedeanUniverse/heisenberg_commutator.lean#L34-L36","doc":"The `q`-Planck constant `ℏ_q = 1 − q⁻¹` — **defined** from the\nsubstrate parameter `q`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}